        "id": "celebrating-seasonal-change",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "A calendar experienced together",
        "content": "Iran’s cultural celebrations make seasonal change a shared experience. Spring provides a setting for renewal; autumn brings thanksgiving for agricultural abundance; winter gatherings create occasions for warmth, conversation and continuity between generations. Yet these occasions do not form a single ceremony repeated under different names. Each has its own timing, characteristic activities and community histories. [s1][s3][s4][s5]\n\nA useful starting point is to distinguish the seasonal occasion from the way a particular household observes it. UNESCO’s descriptions document family gatherings, community performances and agricultural practices, but they also identify variation. A celebration’s cultural importance does not mean that every Iranian participates, or that participation has an identical religious or personal meaning. Read these descriptions as introductions to living practices rather than instructions for a universally correct performance. [s1][s3][s4][s5]",
